        "6. Invite questions and decide on a next step.\nDo not pressure the prospect. If the fit is weak, say so.\n12.3 Beginner-safe pilot principles\nA pilot should:\n- Be small enough to deliver well.\n- Have a written scope.\n- Use agreed inputs and deadlines.\n- Include a defined revision limit.\n- Avoid promising outcomes outside your control.\n- State the price and payment terms clearly.\n- Explain how the client can approve or reject the work.\n- Obtain permission before using client materials in a portfolio.\nIf you cannot yet deliver the proposed work reliably, practise more or offer a smaller scope. Do not take payment for a service you are not prepared to perform."
