        "The source's “AI working while you sleep” idea is most useful when broken into bounded tasks with defined inputs and outputs.\n14.1 Night-time tasks that can be prepared in advance\nTask\tInput\tExpected output\tHuman review\nOpportunity scan\tMarket, skills, time, filters\tShortlist with evidence\tVerify evidence and select one\nProspect research\tICP and buying signals\tQualified prospect records\tCheck fit and source quality\nSample preparation\tBrand context and creative brief\tDraft concepts\tReview originality, accuracy, brand fit\nOutreach drafts\tProspect facts and offer\tPersonalised drafts\tVerify and approve every message\nWebsite copy\tOffer, audience, samples\tDraft landing-page content\tCheck claims and clarity\nInbox summary\tAuthorised email access\tCategorised reply summary\tDecide and send responses\nWeekly review\tActivity and outcome data\tSummary and suggested adjustments\tMake business decisions",
        "14.2 Write task instructions like an employee brief\nEvery recurring task should define:\n- Goal: what outcome is needed?\n- Context: what does the agent need to know?\n- Inputs: which files, links, or data may it use?\n- Method: what steps should it follow?\n- Output: what format should it produce?\n- Quality bar: what makes the result acceptable?\n- Limits: what must it never do?\n- Escalation: when should it stop and ask you?\n14.3 Example: overnight prospect research task\nGoal: prepare a shortlist of relevant companies for tomorrow's review.",
